  <prompt>
    Implement **Rung 4** of the Association Engine: a semantic-match rung that, when deterministic rungs 0–3 do not produce a high-confidence match, runs the extracted terms from the normalized envelope through hybrid search over `RecordSearchService` / the `spaarke-records-index` to find fuzzy candidates for the eight target entities (with FR-14 emphasis on matter / project / invoice / organization). Each candidate carries a `confidenceScore` + `matchReasons[]`.

    Rung 4 emits **`Suggested`-tier results only** — it NEVER auto-files (per FR-11 + owner override: only deterministic rungs 0–3 at ≥0.85 auto-file; AI/semantic rungs always land as `Suggested`/`Ambiguous`). Match reasons are recorded in the per-attribute provenance (`sprk_associationprovenance` JSON) so the W4 review surface (task 042) can show the reviewer why a record was suggested.

    Requirements (FR-14):
    - Implement the rung against the engine's rung interface + normalized envelope (established in W1 task 011) — the rung receives the envelope (`{ from, to[], subject, bodyText, ... }`), never `Microsoft.Graph.Message`.
    - Extract query terms from subject + bodyText (and known structured tokens); run hybrid (vector + keyword) search via `RecordSearchService` over `spaarke-records-index`.
    - Map hits → `confidenceScore` (normalized to the engine's 0–1 confidence scale) + `matchReasons[]` (e.g. "subject term 'Acme v. Smith' matched matter name", "sender org domain matched").
    - Emit results as `Suggested` (never `Resolved`); write provenance per match; respect ADR-024 regarding targets (`sprk_organization` for org — never `account`).
    - Cost containment (NFR-05): rung 4 fires ONLY when deterministic rungs miss / are ambiguous; cache per ADR-014; stay within the ADR-016 budget. Per-rung telemetry is added in task 032 — expose the hooks (timing, hit-count, fired/skipped) it will consume.
    - Reuse existing search infrastructure — do NOT build a new index or a second search client. Answer the Component Justification §11 three-question template in the PR (Existing / Extension / Cost-of-doing-nothing).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer authoritative on `Services/Communication/` and the Association Engine; familiar with `RecordSearchService` / Azure AI Search hybrid query, ADR-013 (AI PublicContracts facade), ADR-024 (regarding family), ADR-016/014 (AI budget/cache), and the binding `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` governance checklist.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A rung-4 semantic-match component plugs into the Association Engine, fires only on deterministic miss/ambiguity, returns fuzzy candidates with `confidenceScore` + `matchReasons[]` for the eight targets, emits `Suggested`-tier only (never auto-files), and writes match reasons into `sprk_associationprovenance`. Uses the existing `RecordSearchService`/`spaarke-records-index` (no new index). Build + tests green; publish-size delta + CVE reported; Placement Justification stated; `/conflict-check` clean.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      W1 refactored `IncomingAssociationResolver` into the Association Engine over a normalized envelope with a rung interface + per-attribute confidence + provenance (task 011), and shipped deterministic rungs 0–3 (tasks 012–014) + confidence→status mapping with auto-file for deterministic ≥0.85 (task 015, ADR-018 kill-switch). Rung 4 is the first non-deterministic rung; it and rung 5 (task 031) are the only rungs allowed to fire on ambiguity/miss, and neither may auto-file.

      FR-11 ladder: deterministic ≥0.85 → `Resolved` (auto-file); 0.50–0.85 OR any AI/semantic rung → `Suggested`; &lt;0.50/none → `Pending Review`; conflicting high-confidence → `Ambiguous`. Rung 4 always lands in the `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` bucket regardless of score.

      Existing infra to reuse (Component Justification §11): `RecordSearchService`, `spaarke-records-index`, `SearchIndexNameResolver` (index-name resolution; W7 task 075 tokenizes names). Do NOT introduce a new index or search client.
    </background>
