  <steps>
    <step order="1">Run `/conflict-check` (BFF hot-path). Load `bff-extensions.md`. Read the W1 rung interface + engine (task 011 output) + the confidence→status mapping (task 015) to confirm the contract rung 4 must satisfy.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `RecordSearchService` + `spaarke-records-index` usage (hybrid query shape, `SearchIndexNameResolver`) and the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade surface for search capability. Confirm the reuse boundary (no new index).</step>
    <step order="3">Design the rung: term-extraction from the envelope (subject + bodyText + structured tokens) → hybrid search → candidate mapping to the eight target entities with `confidenceScore` (normalized 0–1) + `matchReasons[]`. Document the Component Justification §11 answers.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the rung 4 component in `Services/Communication/` implementing the engine rung interface; fire ONLY when rungs 0–3 miss/are ambiguous. Emit `Suggested`-tier results; write `matchReasons` into `sprk_associationprovenance`. Enforce ADR-024 org→`sprk_organization`.</step>
    <step order="5">Wire ADR-014 cache + ADR-016 budget on the search call; expose telemetry hooks (fired/skipped, latency, hit-count, per-target) for task 032. Register via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010); if feature-gated, provide an ADR-032 Null-Object.</step>
    <step order="6">Add/adjust engine wiring so rung 4 runs after deterministic rungs and its `Suggested` results never flip to `Resolved`/auto-file.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (clean) + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication` (existing green; rung-4 unit tests land in task 032).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: invoke `code-review` on the diff; invoke `adr-check` against ADR-045, ADR-024, ADR-013, ADR-016, ADR-014, ADR-032 + `spec.md`. Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 030 ✅; confirm 032 dependency satisfied.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute protocol: status → completed; record decisions (term-extraction strategy, score normalization, fire-gate).</step>
  </steps>

